Aim
To simulate a supermarket billing system using GPSS.

Theory
A Supermarket System simulation is used to study customer movement through billing counters in a shopping environment.
Customers arrive at the supermarket and join the billing queue. When the billing counter becomes available, customers are served and then leave the system.
The GENERATE block creates customers. The QUEUE block stores customers waiting for billing. The SEIZE block allocates the billing counter.
The ADVANCE block represents billing time, while the RELEASE block frees the counter after service.

This experiment helps in analyzing:

Billing counter utilization
Customer waiting time
Queue performance
Service efficiency

Applications:

Shopping malls
Retail stores
Supermarkets
Billing systems


Conclusion
Thus, the supermarket billing system was successfully simulated using GPSS. The experiment demonstrated queue handling and billing counter operations in a supermarket environment.
